Creative dead ends
  1. The initial segment already has full measure, but exposes the unit layer at a/14.
  2. A single 14-gate protects that unit layer and immediately opens positive gaps.
  3. Adding more gates worsens the leak; gate overload is not a viable cover architecture.
  4. S367 residue near-blocker lifts do not become interval counterexamples; repeated residues leak.
  5. Greedy and mutation pressure find dense covers, but exact audits still expose gaps or boundary witnesses.

New disproof idea worth keeping
  Instead of choosing speeds first, solve for a directed endpoint-protection cycle on the
  unit layer plus one higher quotient layer, then realize that cycle by speeds.  The
  speed-first searches repeatedly pay for unit protection by creating higher-denominator
  leaks, so the next counterexample attempt should prescribe the protection graph first.
